Z||000007||ChadMan||09-15-2001||09:35 AM||||Pretty empty threat from a government that doesn't even have the support of its people.  There are still Afghan rebels in the northern end of the country trying to resist the Taliban by force.<P>The Russians wanted to conquer Afghanistan, so the Afghans fought with everything they had (with more than a little help from us).  Afghans might lay down their lives for their homeland, but how many will fight to the death to protect the Taliban?  Remember the Gulf War, in which so many Iraqis forced to fight by Saddam threw down their guns and surrendered?  The Iraqis knew we weren't there to take over their homeland forever and I think the Afghans will know the same thing.<P>I think the Taliban will be gone by this time next year.||||reg||8
